        "id": "p8-q48-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $\\angle XQP$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$45^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Since $XQ\\parallel OR$, $\\angle OQX=45^\\circ$. The right angle at $Q$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\angle XQP&=90^\\circ-\\angle OQX\\\\\n\\angle XQP&=90^\\circ-45^\\circ\\\\\n\\angle XQP&=45^\\circ.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q48-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the exact length of $PQ$ and $OQ$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p8-q48-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "PQ=\\frac12,\\qquad OQ=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}.",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p8-q48-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use sine and cosine of ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "30^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " in right-angled triangle ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "OPQ",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\nPQ&=OP\\sin30^\\circ\\\\\nPQ&=1\\times\\frac12\\\\\nPQ&=\\frac12\\\\\nOQ&=OP\\cos30^\\circ\\\\\nOQ&=1\\times\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\nOQ&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q48-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, deduce that $\\sin75^\\circ=\\dfrac{\\sqrt2+\\sqrt6}{4}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p8-q48-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sin75^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt2+\\sqrt6}{4}.",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p8-q48-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Find ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "PX=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{4}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "QR=\\frac{\\sqrt6}{4}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; then use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "PY=PX+QR",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sin75^\\circ=\\frac{PY}{OP}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\nPX&=PQ\\sin45^\\circ\\\\\nPX&=\\frac12\\times\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\\\\nPX&=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{4}\\\\\nQR&=OQ\\sin45^\\circ\\\\\nQR&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\times\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\\\\nQR&=\\frac{\\sqrt6}{4}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nSince $XYRQ$ is a rectangle, $XY=QR$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nPY&=PX+XY\\\\\nPY&=PX+QR\\\\\nPY&=\\frac{\\sqrt2+\\sqrt6}{4}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nIn right-angled triangle $OPY$, $\\angle POY=30^\\circ+45^\\circ=75^\\circ$ and $OP=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\sin75^\\circ&=\\frac{PY}{OP}\\\\\n\\sin75^\\circ&=\\frac{\\sqrt2+\\sqrt6}{4}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 116
      }
    ]
